ibis: read ast.Constant.value rather than falling back to .n

The fallback is never needed and is always evaluated: Python computes the
default argument of getattr() eagerly, so node.n is read for every constant
in a template expression. ast.Constant.n was deprecated in Python 3.8 and
removed in 3.14, which Kodi 21 links against here - so the read raises
AttributeError, a bare `except: pass` in _parse_primary_expr swallows it, and
the parser reports the expression as unparsable:

  ibis.errors.TemplateSyntaxError: Template 'script-plex-playlist.xml.tpl',
  line 169: Unparsable expression '132+63'.

That kills the addon at startup on any template doing arithmetic, which
includes script-plex-playlist.xml.tpl and script-plex-episodes.xml.tpl.

Upstream: https://github.com/pannal/plex-for-kodi
Applies to 0.7.9-rev4 and 1.0.6 alike.

--- a/lib/_included_packages/ibis/nodes.py
+++ b/lib/_included_packages/ibis/nodes.py
@@ -105,7 +105,7 @@
         if isinstance(node, ast.Expression):
             return _eval(node.body)
         if isinstance(node, utils.Constant):
-            return getattr(node, 'value', getattr(node, 'n'))
+            return node.value
         if isinstance(node, ast.Name):
             return node.id
         if isinstance(node, ast.BinOp):
